  "answer": "All three live path guards on this worktree compare STRINGS (or pathlib parts) rather than Windows-resolved identities. platform/plugin/payload.py:AllowRule.matches allowlists by fnmatch.fnmatch(rel, glob) with no 8.3/trailing-dot fold: the long hook path is ACCEPT under glob C:/Program Files/app/hooks/*, the 8.3 alias C:\\PROGRA~1\\app\\HOOKS~1\\HOOK~1.PY is REJECT (false deny of the same file). tools/command-center/reconcile_delivery.py:_is_declaring_doc excludes by rel == entry or rel.startswith(entry): command-center/WORK-UNIT-CATALOG.json is REJECT (excluded), the 8.3 form COMMAN~1/WORK-U~1.JSO is ACCEPT (the exclude list misses the same identity). Trailing-dot on that basename still startswith the exact entry, so that alias does not slip this particular deny. tools/command-center/render.py write_all is bounded in test_write_all_does_not_touch_the_real_repo by `root in path.parents`: an 8.3 in-root path is REJECT (not seen as inside the root). A string-comparing control deny-guard keyed on C:\\Program Files\\app\\secret.txt ACCEPTs both secret.txt. and C:\\PROGRA~1\\app\\SECRET~1.TXT, proving the probe can see the hole; the canonical twin REJECTs both after win_identity().",
