  "question": "Windows silently normalises a trailing dot or space away, so a blob recorded as `hook.py.` checks out as `hook.py`, and it exposes legacy 8.3 aliases so `PROGRA~1\\x` and `Program Files\\x` are ONE file reachable by two different strings. Target: prove that every path allowlist, deny-guard and repo-root containment check resolves to a canonical real path before comparing, so neither alias slips past. Question: which guard on this estate compares path STRINGS rather than resolved identities? (Reserved device names are a different normalisation defect and are owned by TST-0197 in slice TST-2.)",
